  "source_review_blockers": [],
  "source_review": {
    "packing": "Every RGB colour and five routes (scalar,oldPillow,dispatch,newNumPy,fallbackPillow) exact little-endian truncation; zero dimensions and nonRGB modes preserve return/error parity. No caller mutation.",
    "memory": "Only per-call RGB bytes/output/scratch; no global mutable arrays. Previously measured519650bytes traced peak at240x240 and760bytes retained after1000calls. Imported NumPy resident memory measured separately by root.",
    "concurrency": "64 concurrent calls over8threads byte-identical; UI frame drawing/write/backlight remain synchronous.",
    "warmup": "Updated final delta: constructor creates no task; loading schedules only after first successful synchronous framebuffer write and backlight. Failed writes/backlight never schedule. Owned async task imports dependency in worker only, adopts immutable function only on live instance. Closed guard+task cancel prevent delayed swap; one ever-task prevents retries after failures/cancellation; no-loop retainsPillow. MissingNumPy quiet exact cached fallback; unexpected dependency failure logs once per display and staysPillow. Two independent blocked-worker cases preserved frame bytes, main-thread framebuffer I/O and20heartbeat yields.",
    "startup": "Post-firstpaint scheduling avoids NumPy worker competition during initial draw. ActualPi startup/firstpack/input evidence remains pending."
  },
